---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Projects | Byron David Lencrerot III" description="Software projects by Byron David Lencrerot III, including PresiCompare, a historical data analysis platform, and Huddle Up, a community coordination mobile application.">
  <div class="projects-page">
    <header class="project-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">SELECTED SOFTWARE PROJECTS <span> / 02</span></p>
      <h1>Ideas, engineered<br /><span>into applications.</span></h1>
      <p class="intro-copy">I build software that helps people explore information, make sense of complex data, and bring people together. These projects reflect two different challenges: designing a data-driven research platform and engineering a community-first mobile experience.</p>
      <div class="intro-meta">
        <span><i class="status-dot"></i> Independent development</span>
        <span>Web platforms / Mobile applications / APIs / Data systems</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="case-study presi" aria-labelledby="presicompare-title">
      <div class="case-index">
        <span class="index-number">01</span>
        <span class="case-status"><i class="status-dot"></i> LIVE WEBSITE</span>
      </div>
      <div class="case-content">
        <div class="case-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">DATA • HISTORY • PUBLIC INFORMATION</p>
            <h2 id="presicompare-title">PresiCompare</h2>
          </div>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://presicompare.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit live site <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="case-lede">A data-driven historical analysis platform that organizes public statistics around U.S. presidential terms, helping people examine trends and compare equivalent periods without assigning political scores or declaring a winner.</p>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <article class="feature">
            <span class="feature-number">01 / COLLECT</span>
            <h3>Public data pipeline</h3>
            <p>Imports economic and labor statistics from configured data providers, normalizes observations, and stores their dates, values, metrics, and source context.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="feature">
            <span class="feature-number">02 / ORGANIZE</span>
            <h3>Presidential-term alignment</h3>
            <p>Models each presidential term separately and organizes observations by relative presidential year while retaining the actual calendar period.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="feature">
            <span class="feature-number">03 / EXPLORE</span>
            <h3>Comparison and discovery</h3>
            <p>Provides a web interface for comparing selected terms and exploring historical metrics through structured results, tables, and visualizations.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="architecture">
          <div class="architecture-label">SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE</div>
          <div class="architecture-flow">
            <span>Government data sources</span><b>→</b>
            <span>.NET importer</span><b>→</b>
            <span>SQL Server</span><b>→</b>
            <span>ASP.NET Core API</span><b>→</b>
            <span>Blazor web app</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="project-footer">
          <div class="stack-block">
            <span class="eyebrow">TECHNOLOGY</span>
            <div class="tag-row">
              <span class="tag">C#</span><span class="tag">.NET 9</span><span class="tag">ASP.NET Core</span><span class="tag">Blazor</span><span class="tag">Entity Framework Core</span><span class="tag">SQL Server 2022</span><span class="tag">Docker</span><span class="tag">GitHub Actions</span><span class="tag">Ubuntu</span><span class="tag">Cloudflare Tunnel</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="repo-note"><span class="eyebrow">PROJECT ACCESS</span><p>The public website is live. The source repository is private.</p></div>
        </div>
        <aside class="scope-note"><strong>Data integrity matters.</strong> PresiCompare presents source-attributed observations for users to interpret. It does not claim that a president personally caused every change, and configured metrics are not necessarily all fully populated.</aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="huddle-up" class="case-study huddle" aria-labelledby="huddle-title">
      <div class="case-index">
        <span class="index-number">02</span>
        <span class="case-status"><i class="status-dot in-progress"></i> IN DEVELOPMENT</span>
      </div>
      <div class="case-content">
        <div class="case-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">COMMUNITIES • EVENTS • COORDINATION</p>
            <h2 id="huddle-title">Huddle Up</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="platform-label">Mobile-first product</span>
        </div>
        <p class="case-lede">A community platform designed to help people organize activities, coordinate decisions, share important information, and stay connected in one place. Huddle Up is built for many kinds of communities, not only families.</p>
        <div class="community-types" aria-label="Examples of communities">
          <span>Family</span><span>Friends</span><span>Sports</span><span>Neighborhoods</span><span>Education</span><span>Professional groups</span><span>Clubs &amp; interests</span><span>And more</span>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid huddle-features">
          <article class="feature">
            <span class="feature-number">01 / CONNECT</span>
            <h3>Communities and membership</h3>
            <p>Community creation, membership, Admin and Member roles, invitation codes, discoverability settings, and approval-based join requests form the community model.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="feature">
            <span class="feature-number">02 / ORGANIZE</span>
            <h3>Events and Kickbacks</h3>
            <p>Events support planned activities. Kickbacks are intended for spontaneous gatherings, with a faster, more casual flow than a scheduled event.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="feature">
            <span class="feature-number">03 / PARTICIPATE</span>
            <h3>Polls and Announcements</h3>
            <p>Polls give communities a way to gather input, while Announcements provide a place for community information and updates.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="architecture">
          <div class="architecture-label">APPLICATION ARCHITECTURE</div>
          <div class="architecture-flow huddle-flow">
            <span>Expo / React Native mobile app</span><b>↔</b>
            <span>ASP.NET Core API</span><b>↔</b>
            <span>Relational database / EF Core</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="project-footer">
          <div class="stack-block">
            <span class="eyebrow">TECHNOLOGY</span>
            <div class="tag-row">
              <span class="tag">React Native</span><span class="tag">Expo</span><span class="tag">TypeScript</span><span class="tag">Expo Router</span><span class="tag">ASP.NET Core</span><span class="tag">C#</span><span class="tag">Entity Framework Core</span><span class="tag">REST API</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="repo-note"><span class="eyebrow">PROJECT ACCESS</span><p>The code repository is private. Release readiness and all end-to-end workflows remain subject to validation.</p></div>
        </div>
        <aside class="scope-note"><strong>Current engineering priority.</strong> Protecting a reliable baseline, validating existing workflows, and resolving known issues before expanding the feature set. Planned or incomplete functionality is not presented as release-ready.</aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing-panel">
      <p class="eyebrow">HOW I APPROACH BUILDING</p>
      <h2>Make the system work.<br /><span>Make the details trustworthy.</span></h2>
      <p>Across both projects, I focus on the connection between the user experience and the systems behind it: data integrity, clear responsibilities between application layers, maintainable architecture, and validating real behavior rather than assuming that a screen or build proves a feature is complete.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(body){background:#fff}
  .projects-page{width:min(1160px,calc(100% - 72px));margin:0 auto;padding:70px 0 100px;color:#17191d}
  .project-intro{padding:0 0 42px;border-bottom:1px solid #d9dce0}
  .eyebrow{margin:0 0 15px;font-size:.65rem;line-height:1.5;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.15em;color:#737982}
  .eyebrow span{color:#a0a4aa}
  .project-intro h1{font-size:clamp(3.1rem,7vw,6.7rem);line-height:.94;letter-spacing:-.075em;font-weight:650;margin:0 0 26px}
  .project-intro h1 span,.closing-panel h2 span{color:#858b93}
  .intro-copy{max-width:760px;font-size:1.06rem;line-height:1.85;color:#5c626a;margin:0}
  .intro-meta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-top:32px;padding-top:17px;border-top:1px solid #e3e5e8;font-size:.72rem;color:#686e76}
  .status-dot{display:inline-block;width:7px;height:7px;background:#3e775a;border-radius:50%;margin-right:8px;vertical-align:1px}
  .status-dot.in-progress{background:#b28b43}
  .case-study{display:grid;grid-template-columns:170px minmax(0,1fr);gap:38px;padding:52px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #d9dce0}
  .case-index{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:17px;padding-top:4px}
  .index-number{font-size:3.4rem;line-height:1;font-weight:300;letter-spacing:-.08em;color:#a0a5ac}
  .case-status{font-size:.6rem;letter-spacing:.11em;font-weight:750;color:#656b73;white-space:nowrap}
  .case-content{min-width:0}
  .case-heading{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:space-between;gap:22px;margin-bottom:20px}
  .case-heading .eyebrow{margin-bottom:9px}
  .case-heading h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.1rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:0;font-weight:650}
  .case-lede{max-width:850px;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.85;color:#50565e;margin:0 0 28px}
  .text-link{display:inline-flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;white-space:nowrap;padding:12px 15px;background:#111214;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.72rem;font-weight:700}
  .text-link:hover{background:#3b3e43}
  .platform-label{font-size:.7rem;color:#666d75;border:1px solid #d9dce0;padding:10px 12px;white-space:nowrap}
  .feature-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));border-top:1px solid #d9dce0;border-bottom:1px solid #d9dce0}
  .feature{padding:20px 18px 22px 0}
  .feature+.feature{border-left:1px solid #d9dce0;padding-left:18px}
  .feature-number{display:block;font-size:.58rem;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#858b92;margin-bottom:15px}
  .feature h3{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.35;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 9px}
  .feature p{font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.8;color:#626871;margin:0}
  .architecture{margin-top:27px;padding:20px 22px;background:#f5f6f7;border:1px solid #e4e6e9}
  .architecture-label{font-size:.59rem;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.13em;color:#777d85;margin-bottom:15px}
  .architecture-flow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .architecture-flow span{font-size:.7rem;font-weight:650;line-height:1.5;padding:9px 11px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d8dce0;color:#383d44}
  .architecture-flow b{font-size:.85rem;color:#8a9097;font-weight:500}
  .project-footer{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.6fr) minmax(180px,1fr);gap:30px;margin-top:27px}
  .stack-block .eyebrow,.repo-note .eyebrow{margin-bottom:10px}
  .tag-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:7px}
  .tag{font-size:.65rem;font-weight:650;padding:7px 9px;border:1px solid #d8dce0;color:#555b63}
  .repo-note{border-left:1px solid #d9dce0;padding-left:22px}
  .repo-note p{font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.75;color:#646a72;margin:0}
  .scope-note{margin-top:24px;padding:15px 17px;border-left:3px solid #a9afb6;background:#f7f8f9;font-size:.77rem;line-height:1.8;color:#5b6169}
  .scope-note strong{color:#25292e}
  .community-types{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:7px;margin:-8px 0 27px}
  .community-types span{font-size:.68rem;color:#50565e;background:#f2f3f4;padding:7px 10px}
  .closing-panel{margin-top:52px;padding:34px;background:#111214;color:#fff}
  .closing-panel .eyebrow{color:#b7bbc1}
  .closing-panel h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3.8rem);line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:0 0 20px}
  .closing-panel>p:last-child{max-width:800px;color:#c6c9ce;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.9;margin:0}
  @media(max-width:800px){.projects-page{width:calc(100% - 40px);padding:48px 0 70px}.case-study{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:22px;padding:38px 0}.case-index{flex-direction:row;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between}.index-number{font-size:2.3rem}.feature-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.feature,.feature+.feature{padding:17px 0;border-left:0}.feature+.feature{border-top:1px solid #d9dce0}.project-footer{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:22px}.repo-note{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid #d9dce0;padding:18px 0 0}.architecture-flow{align-items:stretch;flex-direction:column}.architecture-flow b{transform:rotate(90deg);align-self:center}.case-heading{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}.intro-meta{flex-direction:column}.closing-panel{padding:24px}}

  .project-intro{position:relative;isolation:isolate;background-image:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(16,18,20,.97) 0%,rgba(16,18,20,.92) 42%,rgba(16,18,20,.58) 100%),url('/images/engineering-workspace.png');background-size:cover;background-position:center 52%;border-bottom:1px solid #363c42}
  .project-intro h1{font-size:clamp(3.4rem,7vw,6.5rem);max-width:850px}
  .case-study{background:#f5f6f7}
  .case-study:nth-of-type(odd){background:#eceff1}
  .case-content{max-width:100%}
  .case-heading h2{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5vw,4.5rem);letter-spacing:-.065em}
  .case-index{border-right:1px solid #cdd2d7}
  .case-study .case-content{padding-bottom:10px}

</style>
